Wix is one of the most popular website builders around, and it's easy to see why. The drag-and-drop editor looks straightforward, the free plan gets you started quickly, and you don't need any technical knowledge.

But for a small business trying to rank on Google and generate real enquiries, Wix has limitations that aren't obvious when you first sign up.

## What you get with Wix

The free plan puts Wix branding on your site and gives you a Wix subdomain (yourbusiness.wixsite.com/yoursite). To remove the branding and get your own domain, you need a paid plan — starting around £13/month but rising to £22–£27/month for anything practical.

The editor is flexible but cluttered. There are hundreds of templates, thousands of apps, and a lot of decisions to make. For a business owner who just wants to get online, it's more work than it sounds.

## The SEO problem with Wix

Wix has improved its SEO over the years, but it still has real limitations compared to a purpose-built professional site:

- Pages can be slower to load, especially when you add apps and animations
- Site structure is harder to optimise for local search
- You're limited in how you control URLs, metadata, and technical SEO elements
- Wix-hosted sites share infrastructure — you're not on your own hosting environment

For a local business targeting searches like "roofer Cardiff" or "electrician Merthyr Tydfil", that SEO disadvantage compounds over time.

## The hidden cost: your time

The real cost of Wix isn't the monthly fee — it's the hours you spend building and maintaining it. Getting something that looks professional, loads fast, and is set up correctly for SEO is genuinely time-consuming if you're not a web designer. Most small business owners end up with something that looks generic after a full weekend of work.

Then there's ongoing maintenance. When something breaks or needs updating, that's all on you.

## What a managed website gives you instead

Our [Managed Starter Website](/services/managed-starter-websites/) starts from £20/month inc. VAT and includes a properly built website, your domain, hosting, and full management. You don't build it — we build it for you, with a fast turnaround and without cutting corners on quality.

New pages are added every month based on your tier — 5, 10, or unlimited pages — so your site keeps growing while you focus on running your business. Those pages are included with the website plan separately from any SEO package. Small changes are included — just ask. No technical involvement on your end.

Compared to a Wix premium plan, you're paying a similar amount for something that's been built to rank, not just built to exist.

## Which is right for you?

If you enjoy building websites and have the time to invest in learning the platform, Wix can work. But for most small business owners — especially those where local search visibility matters — the time cost and SEO limitations make it a poor long-term choice.

